From 1fcbf0fb07500afe783aec64d1857949ed3b84ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:59:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] WowCraft: Minecraft's blocks and bodies in their own
 colours

blocks.rs uploaded the block atlas and entity textures as Rgba8UnormSrgb and turned Minecraft's
vertex tints to linear, but WoW's world framebuffer holds gamma bytes (WoW's own textures are
un-encoded, unlit materials write their colour raw, FFXGlow decodes once), so every block, our
body and the scene came out decoded twice. Measured live with mod/test/VisualMinecraft's atlas
(ffxGlow off, Northshire, sky light 15): a sunlit grass top face (atlas 90,170,60) drew
26,103,12 and a north dirt face (138,96,67 x 0.8) 52,24,12; the overlay's hotbar in the same
shot read its exact bytes, so the capture is true.

- Textures upload un-encoded (Rgba8Unorm), as WoW's and mc_body's do.
- Vertex tints and Minecraft's light multiply the bytes raw; srgb_to_linear goes.
- The fishing line's grey passes raw (linear_rgba), as the overhead names' colours do.
- The vertex test uses a real tint (plains grass) and a new test checks the texture format.

After: the top face draws 90,169,60 (second texel 68,138,46, exact), the north faces
111,77,53 and the west faces 82,58,41 (138,96,67 x 0.6 = 83,58,40).

Verified: cargo test --release -p benilla-app --no-default-features --lib wowcraft (38);
cargo build --release -p benilla --no-default-features; the live run above, before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
